 a well-known former county executive, seeks reelection against Republican Mike LiPetri. Suozzi holds a decisive financial advantage, with roughly $5.7 million on hand to LiPetri's $0.7 million, and has campaigned on moderate, bipartisan themes including a U.S. Chamber award and local constituent work. Expert raters mostly place the race at Lean D or Likely D, and prediction markets price Suozzi's chances in the high 80s.\nThe main source of drama is outside spending: a Trump-affiliated super PAC has put about $8 million into ads attacking Suozzi over stock trading, and GOP efforts to boost LiPetri have intensified. With no public general-election polls, the forecast leans on fundamentals and ratings, pointing to a Suozzi win with meaningful but not overwhelming confidence.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8955, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}]}